      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to introduce 79 Walnut Rise, Courtlands a fantastic Four-bedroom Semi Detached family home ideally positioned in one of Drumcondra's most sought-after residential estates, just off Griffith Avenue.\nCourtlands is an award-winning residential estate within walking distance to the wide variety of amenities that Drumcondra, Phibsborough and Glasnevin have to offer, all practically on your doorstep and just a short distance from the City Centre. This superb home is within comfortable walking distance of the Botanic Gardens, Griffith Park, Na Fianna GAA Club and Croke Park. The property is situated close to both the Bon Secours and Mater hospitals. Third level colleges include Dublin City University and St Patrick s Teacher Training College which are within easy walking distance; Trinity College Dublin and University College Dublin are both on direct bus routes. This fantastic home is located within a great catchment of both primary and secondary schools and is serviced by an excellent bus route offering a high frequency service to the City Centre. The M50 and Dublin Airport are also easily accessible making this a most strategically positioned home in this fantastic neighbourhood, renowned for its strong sense of community.\nBright and spacious internal accommodation of c. 117 sq.m comprises an entrance hallway, large living room to front with feature fireplace, dining room, storage closet and a fully fitted kitchen. Upstairs hosts four generous bedrooms and a family bathroom. This superb family home comes to the market in good condition throughout and has the benefit of gas fired central heating, front driveway with large garage and a generous westerly facing rear garden with block built sheds and a gated side entrance.\nThe property's new owner will have the opportunity to apply their own stamp and lay down roots in one of Dublin 9's most sought after and family-oriented locations where properties rarely come to the market. An opportunity not to be missed; Contact our Northside office on 01-6995050 for further information or to arrange viewing!!\n\nAdditional Features;\n<ul>\n <li>Eligible for VACANT PROPERTY REFURBISHMENT GRANT</li>\n <li>c. 117 sq.m</li>\n <li>BER: C</li>\n <li>4 bed 1 bath</li>\n <li>Semi Detached family home</li>\n <li>Front driveway with Large garage</li>\n <li>Gas fired central heating</li>\n <li>Large Westerly facing rear garden</li>\n <li>Generous sized bedrooms</li>\n <li>Highly sought-after location</li>\n <li>Light filled interior</li>\n <li>Excellent primary, secondary schools closeby</li>\n <li>Close to DCU and St. Patricks College</li>\n <li>Easy access to M50 motorway</li>\n <li>Close to National Botanic Gardens</li>\n <li>Excellent transport links nearby</li>\n <li>Bus routes to City Centre and Drumcondra Train station close by</li>\n <li>Within walking distance of Drumcondra, Glasnevin and Phibsborough villages</li>\n <li>Nearby Na Fianna GAA Club, Glasnevin Lawn Tennis Club and Tolka Rovers AFC</li>\n <li>Within 20 minutes' drive to Dublin Airport</li>\n <li>Ideal for first-time buyers, families and investors alike</li>\n <li>Early Viewing is highly advised!!</li>\n</ul>"
      },
